WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.504
-My next guest
is a talented actor

00:00:02.504 --> 00:00:05.371
who stars in the big new film
"Jungle Cruise,"

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.773
which is in theaters
and on Disney+

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:10.343
with premiere access
on July 30th.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.346
Please welcome Edgar Ramirez!

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.948
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:17.884
-♪ Edgar Ramirez,
you can do no wrong ♪

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:22.388
♪ when it comes to fashion,
you got your Versace on ♪

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:26.793
♪ Edgar Ramirez,
you know you can't lose ♪

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:31.096
♪ When you're Aguirre
in that "Jungle Cruise" ♪

00:00:31.096 --> 00:00:37.203
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.105
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.840
-Welcome back.
-Whoa. Thank you so much.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.910
Oh, my God.
This is so, oh, energizing.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.645
Thank you, guys.
-It is. Right?

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.947
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Whoa. See? Wow.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.982
I mean, to be here
back in New York

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:51.283
and back with an audience.

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.853
-I know! It's happening.
It's all good.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.288
-Wow.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.590
-Is this your first time back
in New York since "The Undoing"?

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.559
-Yes.
I mean, I'm just very happy.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.261
"The Undoing" was a love letter
to New York.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.829
It was the last time I was here.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.364
-What would you think?
Because --

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.665
We got so into "The Undoing."
-Thank you.

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:08.467
-I was getting into, like,

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:11.738
heated debates about who did it
and what's going on.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.340
But everyone was -- Everyone
in the world was watching it.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.275
-Yeah.
-And you get Nicole Kidman.

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:18.077
-Yeah, your -- your --

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.647
-She's my friend, yeah.
And -- Yeah, sorry.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.414
-And your --
-Anyway, yeah, it's all good.

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:24.117
-Your would've-been wife.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.218
-Everything's good.
Everything's good.

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:27.987
-You have no idea
how many times

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.355
I've watched that YouTube video.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.791
-Oh, well, you know, after
the first time, you're good.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.159
You know?
-Do you still have cheese

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.328
and crackers to offer ladies
when they're...

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.329
-But Hugh Grant.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.331
-Oh, yeah. He was amazing.

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:41.267
-Yeah, I dated Hugh Grant,
as well,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.835
and no one talks about that.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.804
But everybody was phenomenal.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.039
You were phenomenal
in this thing.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.239
-Thank you very much.
Thank you.

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:49.908
The funny thing is that
I had people --

00:01:49.908 --> 00:01:53.512
a lot of people, you know,
coming to me and saying,

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:55.815
"You were so good
at playing this cop.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:59.586
I mean, we love the show,
and you play them all the time.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.387
I mean, you're so good
at playing them."

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.055
-Playing a cop.
-Playing a cop.

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:05.258
And I would say, "But it's the
first time that I play a cop."

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.693
Like, I've never
played it before.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.394
It was the first time.
-But you're so good at it,

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.996
they think --
-No, but then, yeah.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.131
Talking about -- I've played
a lot of criminals before.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.234
And I remember earlier
in my career, people would say,

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.869
"Aren't you afraid
to get pigeonholed

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.670
because you're playing
these criminals?"

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.606
And I said, "No, I mean,
they're characters,

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.474
and, you know,
they're three-dimensional."

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.742
And now I play one cop,

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.944
and then even journalists
come and say,

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.313
"I mean, you're so well --
you're so good playing them.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.748
You play them all the time."

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.717
It's the only time
that I played a cop.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:34.053
-What's your next role?
-It is a cop.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.356
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.725
-This is how it happens!
You put it out there!

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.659
You put it --
-You put it out there once.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.461
-You put it out there,
and that's it now!

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:43.929
-Exactly.
-No, you've got --

00:02:43.929 --> 00:02:46.098
You've done everything.
I have some photos here.

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:47.967
I just want to know your...
-Oh, my God.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.868
-...stories behind some of your
costars that you've worked with.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.270
Talk to me about De Niro.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.106
-You know, he's a man
of very few words.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:54.941
-Oh, I know.
-You know, right?

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.642
-Yeah, he's been
on the show many times.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.144
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.313
Even in interviews. We've done
a couple of movies together,

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:03.950
and we've been paired up
for junkets,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.718
I mean, for interviews.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.353
And sometimes -- Many times,

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.655
they will come
and ask him questions,

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:12.058
and he would say, like,
"You know what?

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.892
Edgar has a better answer
to that question.

00:03:13.892 --> 00:03:16.629
Edgar, bring it home."

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.231
-How about --
We love Jennifer Garner.

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.399
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:21.734
-Tell me the first thing
that comes to your mind.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.969
-She's a very organized lady.
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:26.239
She's very organized
because she's very busy.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.774
So, you know,
she's a full-time mom.

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:30.109
-Yeah, she's a great mom.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.912
-She's a CEO, she's a business
woman, she's a producer.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.113
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.747
And, of course, a great actress.

00:03:35.747 --> 00:03:38.784
So, she has -- I remember
when we were doing "Yes Day,"

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:42.121
our comedy on Netflix,
last year.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.391
I always saw her during
the breaks with an iCal

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.226
with a computer on the calendar

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.562
and with a planner
that was a notebook.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:53.198
And then I would ask her,
"Jennifer, how do you --

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:55.935
I mean, why do you have --
Isn't one calendar enough?

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.203
I mean, why do you have two?"

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.537
"No, because I have to
correlate them, you know,

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:00.039
like, the bigger events.

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.340
I put them here,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.875
and then there's more things,
I put them here."

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.109
It was an amazing system.

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:06.746
And then she got me
my first planner.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.581
And -- Yeah.
-I'm almost tearing up.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.116
I'm almost --
I'm getting emotional.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.516
-Yeah, no, yeah, yeah.
It's true.

00:04:11.516 --> 00:04:12.685
I have it. I have it.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.420
I mean, I haven't
correlated it yet.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.121
But I have it, man,
and I'm hopeful.

00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:18.557
-Baby steps.
I love how organized.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:21.494
That's great.
And how about this gentleman?

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:22.695
This is Dwayne Johnson.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.163
-Ah, Dwayne Johnson.
-This is Dwayne Johnson.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.832
-He's incredible.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:28.601
You're right. You're right.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.670
That guy, I mean, he lights up
the room when he walks in.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.305
-He really does.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.673
-Yeah, he's so full of
gratitude, and he's great.

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:36.743
You know, he's very,
very compassionate.

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:40.780
I remember when shortly before
we started "Jungle Cruise,"

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.651
I went to Iceland, and I had
an accident and I broke a rib.

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:49.154
So, yeah.
And like two weeks or 10 days

00:04:49.154 --> 00:04:51.991
leading up to starting this
big movie and doing some stunts.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:55.828
And the rib healed. I mean,
thank God it healed quickly.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.297
But I remember when I --
when we started

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:00.199
doing the stunts, and he said,
"Edgar, don't worry.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.801
I got you.
I mean, you have no idea.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.836
Do you have any idea
how many bones I've broken?

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.838
I mean, it's like,
I know exactly how it feels,

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.006
so I'm going to help you."

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.841
And he's that kind of guy.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.275
-Yeah, he's that kind of guy.

00:05:10.275 --> 00:05:13.012
-He's gigantic, too,
so I'm happy that he helped me.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.447
-Well, this movie is giant.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:17.249
"Jungle Cruise." When Disney
does it, they do it giant.

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:18.517
-Yeah. It's big, yeah.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:19.952
It's based on the ride,
and you have all these --

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.820
-The first ride ever made,
by the way, in Disney World.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.389
-In Disney World.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.824
Yeah, yeah, in the mid-'50s.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.191
-And you have a --

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:28.527
You have a giant --
-What is that?

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:31.263
-Well, you have snakes crawling
through your face in this movie.

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:35.234
-Oh, yeah, I know, I know.
And do I love them.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.702
-Yeah. It's pretty creepy.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:38.604
Were you around
any real snakes during this?

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:39.972
-No, no, no. Thank God, no.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:42.541
No, I hate -- I hate --
I don't hate them.

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.710
I'm very respectful of snakes.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.646
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.281
-That is in case
any snakes are watching.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:49.815
-Yeah, I don't -- Yeah, exactly.

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:51.751
I don't want to --
-Very respectful.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.752
-Yeah, I'm very respectful
of snakes,

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:55.554
and I've had
very crazy experiences

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:57.423
with snakes,
you know, like growing up.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.525
We would find snakes
in the backyard,

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:04.697
and we would find snakes
even rolled up in the toilet.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.732
So can you imagine
my level of trauma?

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:08.267
-No.
-Yeah.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.169
But that's what happens
with actors in movies.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.738
Then suddenly,
you are very respectful...

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:14.707
"scared" of snakes.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.409
And then suddenly, yeah,
you're playing

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:18.077
this amazing role,
with Emily Blunt.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.978
-Snakes all over you.
-And snakes all over you.

00:06:19.978 --> 00:06:21.380
-And Emily Blunt, yeah.
-Exactly.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.215
-But that's what acting is,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:24.850
That's what I'm talking about

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:27.119
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-You're one of the best, pal.

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:28.687
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:28.687 --> 00:06:31.256
Here's Edgar Ramirez
in "Jungle Cruise."

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:33.659
Take a look at this.
-What's going on?

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.294
-That's what I was trying
to tell you.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.396
♪♪

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:39.064
[ Snake hissing ]

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:44.002
♪♪

00:06:44.002 --> 00:06:46.272
-No.

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:48.607
♪♪

00:06:48.607 --> 00:06:50.643
-[ Speaking native language ]

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.978
-It's impossible.

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:54.880
♪♪

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.916
-The myth is real.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.095
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:10.095 --> 00:07:14.099
-Edgar Ramirez!
"Jungle Cruise" is in theaters

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:17.870
and on Disney+
with premiere access July 30th.

